WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.554
Managing intrinsic load begins with sequencing.

2
00:00:02.554 --> 00:00:12.343
Learners usually benefit from moving from simple to complex, from prerequisite knowledge to combined performance, and from clear examples to more varied cases.

3
00:00:12.343 --> 00:00:21.706
When instruction begins with the full complexity of a task, beginners may not know which elements matter or how the parts relate.

4
00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:25.111
Sequencing gives them a path into the domain.

5
00:00:25.111 --> 00:00:28.090
Chunking and scaffolding help learners handle complexity.

6
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.921
A chunk groups related information into a meaningful unit.

7
00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:36.177
A scaffold provides temporary support while the learner builds capability.

8
00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:49.796
In practice, this might mean teaching one decision rule before combining it with exceptions, showing one data flow before introducing multiple systems, or giving learners a checklist before expecting fluent independent performance.

9
00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:54.053
Worked examples and partially completed examples are especially useful early.

10
00:00:54.053 --> 00:01:01.714
They reduce the need for learners to discover every step while they are still forming the basic schema.

11
00:01:01.714 --> 00:01:07.672
A worked example shows how a task is solved and why the steps matter.

12
00:01:07.672 --> 00:01:17.036
A partially completed example asks learners to finish selected parts, which shifts some responsibility to them without dropping all support at once.

13
00:01:17.036 --> 00:01:19.164
Progressive complexity is the key.

14
00:01:19.164 --> 00:01:25.122
Reduce the number of interacting elements early, then add more as learners gain structure.

15
00:01:25.122 --> 00:01:28.101
This does not mean hiding reality forever.

16
00:01:28.101 --> 00:01:31.932
It means building foundations before expecting full independent performance.

17
00:01:31.932 --> 00:01:40.444
When learners have a stable starting model, later complexity becomes easier to place and less likely to overwhelm working memory.
